045417] [17592186437213 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186437211 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437213 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186437212 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437213 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437213 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437213 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186437208 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437213 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "07041bd7-da85-5245-8203-4f70786b0ce5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437214 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186437213 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437214 #edb/ref 1069 "q-81263" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437214 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437214 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $T([\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}u\\operatorname{ln}⁡v \\\\ {u}^{2}{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437214 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fdaff75b-e0c6-5e92-b720-ea0f3e9d5336" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437214 #edb/ref 1074 "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, we have $x=u\\operatorname{ln}⁡v$ and $y={u}^{2}{v}^{2}.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡v & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =\\frac{u}{v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =2u{v}^{2} & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =2{u}^{2}v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡v & \\frac{u}{v} \\\\ 2u{v}^{2} & 2{u}^{2}v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡v\\cdot 2{u}^{2}v-\\frac{u}{v}\\cdot 2u{v}^{2} \\\\  & =2{u}^{2}v(\\operatorname{ln}⁡v-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
